# Security and resource limits

Retain or add protections for: maximum file size; maximum YAML depth; maximum mapping entries; duplicate-key rejection; alias expansion; package-key length; dependency-reference length; peer-suffix length; patch-suffix length; workspace path length; package-index size; cancellation; bounded allocations.

Fuzz applicable parsers and encoders, including: package identities; scoped names; peer contexts; patches; aliases; protocol references; workspace references; dependency references; graph-key encoding; snapshot encoding; semantic-version declarations; migration loss analysis.

Do not access the registry during: parsing; lock validation; semantic diff; migration dry-run; fixture verification.
